.TH MAGUS 1 "" "magus" "magus Manual"
.SH NAME
magus \- workspace-aware build orchestrator and content-addressed cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magus
.RI [ flags ]\ <subcommand>\ [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
magus is a standalone build orchestrator and content\-addressed cache for
multi\-language monorepos, and an evolution of Mage. It provides workspace\-aware
subcommands for building, testing, linting, and inspecting projects without
requiring Mage to be installed.
.PP
magus reads optional configuration from magus.yaml (XDG, workspace root, or
CWD) and MAGUS_* environment variables. All configuration can be overridden
with CLI flags.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
Global flags are accepted by every subcommand and may appear before or
after the subcommand word. Last\-write\-wins, matching kubectl conventions.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
Workspace root. Default: walk up from cwd until go.mod is found. Must precede the subcommand.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR
Config file path. Default: search for magus.yaml in CWD, workspace root, and $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magus/. Must precede the subcommand.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfmt\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format: text (default), json, yaml, name, jsonl, or template[=<go\-template>]. Honored by subcommands that emit structured data. A template body renders a Go text/template over the same value \-o json emits (field names are the json keys); a bare \-o template with no body lists that output's fields instead of rendering \- the json keys usable in \-o json and \-o template, with each field's type and doc.
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum number of concurrent build steps. 0 means use the configured value (or MAGUS_CONCURRENCY, or concurrency_profile, balanced (min(NumCPU,8)) by default).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log verbosity. Repeat for more detail (\-v, \-vv, \-vvv).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.RS
.TP
\fBls\fR
List all discovered projects. See \fBmagus\-ls\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdescribe\fR
Define a magus concept and list its entities. See \fBmagus\-describe\fR(1).
.TP
\fBwhere\fR
Print the absolute path of a project. See \fBmagus\-where\fR(1).
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Run a target for selected projects. See \fBmagus\-run\fR(1).
.TP
\fBaffected\fR
Run a target for VCS\-diff affected projects. See \fBmagus\-affected\fR(1).
.TP
\fBx\fR
Reproduce an output ref, or pick project + target. See \fBmagus\-x\fR(1).
.TP
\fBclean\fR
Remove declared outputs (regenerable, never sources). See \fBmagus\-clean\fR(1).
.TP
\fBshell\fR
Check a command against this workspace's conventions before running it. See \fBmagus\-shell\fR(1).
.TP
\fBquery\fR
Search the knowledge graph, and retrieve a run's output or journal by id. See \fBmagus\-query\fR(1).
.TP
\fBrefs\fR
List where an ingested code symbol is defined and referenced. See \fBmagus\-refs\fR(1).
.TP
\fBexplain\fR
Show one knowledge\-graph node's context: data, edges, and reach. See \fBmagus\-explain\fR(1).
.TP
\fBpath\fR
Connect two knowledge\-graph nodes: the shortest chain of edges between them. See \fBmagus\-path\fR(1).
.TP
\fBgraph\fR
The workspace's graphs as objects: deps, export, stats. See \fBmagus\-graph\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdiff\fR
Read the working tree's changes in the order they deserve attention. See \fBmagus\-diff\fR(1).
.TP
\fBvcs\fR
Staging and conflict resolution that knows what is generated. See \fBmagus\-vcs\fR(1).
.TP
\fBsession\fR
What magus invocations did and what agents are blocked on: humans read and dispose, hosts write. See \fBmagus\-session\fR(1).
.TP
\fBjob\fR
Fork a job, take it, return it with its result, and verify that result. See \fBmagus\-job\fR(1).
.TP
\fBnotes\fR
Human\-authored notes committed to the repository. See \fBmagus\-notes\fR(1).
.TP
\fBqueue\fR
Merge approved changes through a speculative, partitioned merge queue. See \fBmagus\-queue\fR(1).
.TP
\fBwatch\fR
Emit changed file paths to stdout. See \fBmagus\-watch\fR(1).
.TP
\fBevents\fR
Stream workspace events as JSONL for an integration to consume. See \fBmagus\-events\fR(1).
.TP
\fBserver\fR
Manage the magus server: MCP, the console, APIs and background jobs. See \fBmagus\-server\fR(1).
.TP
\fBbroker\fR
The per\-user process holding this host's capacity and shared services. See \fBmagus\-broker\fR(1).
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Serve MCP over stdio for the agent host that launched it. See \fBmagus\-mcp\fR(1).
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Inspect concurrency pool and configuration. See \fBmagus\-status\fR(1).
.TP
\fBbuzz\fR
Run a Buzz script. See \fBmagus\-buzz\fR(1).
.TP
\fBspell\fR
Build, publish, pull and list spells as OCI artifacts, and pin them in magus.lock. See \fBmagus\-spell\fR(1).
.TP
\fBagent\fR
Manage skills, harnesses, and agent feedback. See \fBmagus\-agent\fR(1).
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Bootstrap a workspace (magus.yaml + magusfile.buzz + merge driver). See \fBmagus\-init\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Validate the workspace. See \fBmagus\-doctor\fR(1).
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
View or update magus configuration. See \fBmagus\-config\fR(1).
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR
Print a shell completion script. See \fBmagus\-completion\fR(1).
.TP
\fBman\fR
Install the man pages embedded in this binary. See \fBmagus\-man\fR(1).
.TP
\fBself\fR
Manage the magus binary (update, install\-shorthand). See \fBmagus\-self\fR(1).
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the client and server versions. See \fBmagus\-version\fR(1).
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.RS
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_DIR\fR
One dir for the entries and the checkout's own files (default: entries shared per repository, the rest in .magus/). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.dir\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_WRITE_ENABLED\fR
When false, replay cache hits but never write new entries, locally or to a remote (default true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.write.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_INCLUDE_OS_ENABLED\fR
When true, this host property keys every cache entry; off by default because a manifest guard already refuses a cross\-platform replay. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.include.os.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_INCLUDE_ARCH_ENABLED\fR
When true, this host property keys every cache entry; off by default because a manifest guard already refuses a cross\-platform replay. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.include.arch.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_SIZE_MB\fR
Disk cap in MB (binary); 0 = unlimited. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.size_mb\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_TRUSTED_KEYS\fR
Base64 Ed25519 public keys a remote artifact must be signed by; required when a backend is wired. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.trusted_keys\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_INSECURE\fR
Disables remote\-cache signature verification: unsigned artifacts are imported and produced with no trust set. A shared cache without signing is a supply\-chain hazard — use only for trusted single\-repo CI, or to validate a backend before minting keys. When true, trusted_keys stops being required and InsecureReason starts. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.insecure\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_INSECURE_REASON\fR
The prose behind Insecure, required whenever it is true. Same rule SkipCacheReason and DriftReason carry: switching off the check that says whether an artifact came from who it claims is a claim about this cache. This file is committed, so the next machine to trust the cache reads the answer here. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.insecure_reason\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_WRITE_ENABLED\fR
When false, write the local tier but never the remote; unset writes the remote when the local tier is written and a signing key is held; true makes remote writes required. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.write.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_MAX_SHARDS\fR
Max parallel shards; \-1 = unlimited (default: 8). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.max_shards\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_RUNNER_POOL_BUDGET\fR
GHA matrix\-level concurrency cap; 0 = no cap. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.runner_pool_budget\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_RECORD_RUNS\fR
Keeps the per\-branch run log (forecast.Run) in the history file: which commit a branch passed or failed a target at, and when. On by default, because `\-\-base last\-passed` reads it and a CI run that cannot find its base gates less than it appears to (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.record_runs\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_ENABLED\fR
The master switch for volatility detection and auto\-retry; false disables all retry logic (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_BOOTSTRAP_SAMPLES\fR
Outcomes below which all failures retry once (default: 20). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.bootstrap_samples\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_MIN_SAMPLES\fR
Minimum outcomes before Wilson\-score gates retry (default: 20). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.min_samples\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_THRESHOLD\fR
Wilson lower\-bound above which a project+target is volatile (default: 0.05). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.threshold\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_ANNOTATE_GHA\fR
Emit ::warning annotations and GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY table (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.annotate_gha\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_ENABLED\fR
Turns OTLP export on; magus connects to Endpoint when true. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT\fR
Host:port; required when Enabled. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.endpoint\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_PROTOCOL\fR
OTLP wire protocol: grpc or http (default: grpc). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.protocol\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_INSECURE\fR
Disable TLS. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.insecure\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_SERVICE_NAME\fR
Resource attribute service.name (default: magus). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.service_name\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_SAMPLE_RATIO\fR
Head\-based sampling ratio; 1.0 = all (default: 1). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.sample_ratio\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_ENABLED\fR
Lets a command hand itself to a running `magus server`; false runs each invocation self\-contained. Default true. With Enabled false an invocation never discovers or adopts the server and hosts its own per\-process pool. Recursive magus calls still forward over a per\-process socket to share the concurrency budget; only the server is opted out of (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_ADDRESS\fR
The unix:// socket `magus server` listens on; empty means server.sock in the runtime dir. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.address\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_IDLE_TTL\fR
Controls workspace eviction in the multi\-workspace server; 0 = default 6h. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.idle_ttl\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_WORKSPACES\fR
The explicit list of workspace roots to serve; non\-empty enables eager union of sandbox policies and rejects out\-of\-list workspaces (MGS2010). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.workspaces\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_ROTATE_ACTIVITIES\fR
Only how often the server CHECKS whether the activity trail is due for a trim; it is not a retention age. The trail rotates on event count instead: 10000 events, with a per\-kind floor that keeps a rare kind's newest entries no matter how loud its neighbors are (see maxEvents and perKindFloor in internal/trail). So there is no age cutoff this field could hand it: an age cutoff would have to decide whether it or the per\-kind floor wins when the two disagree, and that policy does not exist. It runs hourly because a rotate on an already\-small trail costs one stat (default: 1h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.rotate_activities\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_ROTATE_LOGS\fR
Both how often the server checks the run\-log journals AND, since the check doubles as the enforcement, the maximum age a kept journal may reach: a journal older than this is dropped even when the workspace is well under the count (500) and size (2GB) caps those also enforce, and the tightest of the three wins. Weekly by default, because run\-logs otherwise have no age bound at all (default: 168h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.rotate_logs\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_PRUNE_PRESERVED\fR
Only how often the server checks for expired `vcs checkpoint \-\-preserve` captures; it is not the retention window. That window is fixed at 30 days (vcs.preserveRetention) and stays out of this field on purpose: the days a preserved capture survives is a promise the `\-\-preserve` flag itself advertises, and letting a per\-server poll knob also change what gets deleted would make that promise mean whatever this config happened to say (see the rationale on vcs.PrunePreserved). Preserve prunes on its own call too, but only a repository preserved a SECOND time ever reaches that pass, so this scheduled job is what makes the promise hold for a repository preserved once and never again. Daily, since a capture surviving an extra day past the fixed window costs nothing (default: 24h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.prune_preserved\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_SYNC_GRAPH\fR
Reconcile the graph; default 6h (a safety net behind the VCS hook) (default: 6h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.sync_graph\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_CHECK_REVIEW\fR
Notices a merge or a new remark on a review this tree took part in. The only scheduled job that leaves the machine, so its default is the longest here: a pull request merges once, and a remark waiting fifteen minutes costs nobody anything (default: 15m). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.check_review\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_ENABLED\fR
Master switch for VCS\-driven affected detection; false makes affected fall back to all projects (default true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_NAME\fR
Pin VCS by name (git/hg/sl/jj); empty = autodetect. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.name\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_BASE_REF\fR
Sets the default base ref. Per\-VCS overrides use MAGUS_VCS_<NAME>_BASE_REF (dynamic; not a Config field). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.base_ref\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_ENABLED\fR
When false, refuse to start the MCP server (default true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_ADDRESS\fR
Host:port; default 127.0.0.1:7391. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.address\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_HTTP\fR
Serves /mcp on the server's HTTP listener. False leaves the route unmounted while `magus mcp` (stdio) and the server socket keep serving MCP, and the listener keeps the console and health routes. Default true. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.http\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_INSECURE_BIND\fR
Permits a non\-loopback Address. That listener serves bearer tokens over plaintext HTTP, so without it the server refuses to start rather than warn. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.insecure_bind\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONSOLE_ENABLED\fR
When false, the MCP HTTP server does not mount the console's read\-only API and job service (default true when MCP is up). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconsole.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_REPORT_FILTER\fR
Restricts event types via +type/\-type/bare terms; any "+" sets default\-deny. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBreport.filter\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_FORMAT\fR
The log format: pretty, plain, text or json. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.format\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_LEVEL\fR
The minimum log level; "trace" also enables the startup timing table. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.level\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_SILENT\fR
Suppresses progress like \-\-quiet, and additionally bounds the failing\-project dump (tail + path to the full log) and bubbles up only lines a target marks as a notice ("magus:notice:"). Like \-\-quiet it prints a failure's reasoning only at \-v. Normally set via \-s/\-\-silent; MAGUS_LOG_SILENT=1 is the env equivalent. Pointer to distinguish "not set" from explicit false. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.silent\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_STREAM\fR
Shows every target's subprocess output live and interleaved, instead of withholding a passing target's output until it fails. This is deliberately NOT derived from Level: what gets logged and whether a target's own output is withheld are separate questions, and conflating them is why \-v used to ambush people with a wall of concurrent output when they wanted a little more detail. Normally set via \-vv (and implied by \-vvv); MAGUS_LOG_STREAM=1 is the env equivalent. Pointer to distinguish "not set" from explicit false. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.stream\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_HINTS_ENABLED\fR
Controls whether hint messages (actionable nudges) are printed to stderr. Defaults to true. Set hints.enabled: false in magus.yaml or MAGUS_HINTS_ENABLED=false to suppress all hint output. Pointer to distinguish "not set" from explicit false (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBhints.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_WORKSPACES\fR
Additional workspace roots to union into a `\-\-global` knowledge\-graph query (query/explain/path and graph export/stats). Each is loaded and its node IDs are namespaced by the workspace ("<name>//<id>") so IDs from different repos cannot collide. Empty means \-\-global covers only the current workspace. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.workspaces\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_PUBLISHED_REF\fR
The OCI artifact a published knowledge graph is READ from, as <registry>/<repository>:<tag>. Empty (the default) means this workspace pulls nothing and every graph is built locally. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.published_ref\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_MAX_SIZE_MB\fR
A soft cap on the knowledge shard store (<cache>/knowledge). When exceeded after a build, least\-recently\-used shard files are evicted; an evicted shard is restored from the remote cache or rebuilt on the next query. 0 (default) is unlimited: the store self\-reconciles deleted projects, so a cap mainly bounds transient bloat. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.max_size_mb\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_ENABLED\fR
Folds VCS history (last commit, commit count) onto file nodes as the @vcs shard. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_MAX_COMMITS\fR
Bounds the history walk to the most recent N commits. 0 uses a built\-in default; a small value keeps the scan fast on a large repo at the cost of undercounting commits for long\-lived files. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.max_commits\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_AUTHORSHIP\fR
Includes the `author` nodes and `authored` edges (who touched which files) in the graph. Defaults to ON (nil = on): authorship is context that helps an agent, and the edges are already bounded by MaxCommits. Set false to keep only the per\-file vcs_* attrs and omit the author layer (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.authorship\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_DISABLED\fR
Opts out of background auto\-indexing. Auto\-indexing is on by default in the server, so this is the switch to turn it off (e.g. the indexers are not installed and you index in CI instead). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.disabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_QUIET_SECONDS\fR
How long a project's sources must be quiet after the last change before it is re\-indexed, so a burst of edits coalesces into one run. 0 uses a built\-in default. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.quiet_seconds\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS\fR
The minimum time between re\-index runs for one project, a ceiling on how often the indexer fires however often files change. 0 uses a built\-in default. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.min_interval_seconds\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_CALLEES\fR
Fewest callees a function needs before the lens compares it (default: 3). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_callees\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SHARED\fR
Fewest shared callees a pair needs to be reported (default: 4). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_shared\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SCORE\fR
Lowest similarity score in [0,1] the lens reports (default: 0.7). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_score\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SPAN_RATIO\fR
Lowest ratio in [0,1] of the shorter function's span to the longer one's (default: 0.5). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_span_ratio\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_INCLUDE_TESTS\fR
When true, the lens also compares test functions. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.include_tests\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SESSIONS_DISABLED\fR
Opts out entirely, so `graph build` runs no adapter and `\-\-no\-sessions` becomes the permanent answer. The switch to reach for when the transcripts on this machine are not yours to read. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.sessions.disabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_NOTES_SHARED\fR
The workspace\-relative directory holding notes the TEAM has: committed, so git attributes each one to whoever wrote it and review sees every change. Empty disables it entirely: no shard, no verification, no guard rule. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.notes.shared\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_NOTES_PRIVATE\fR
A SECOND notes location, yours rather than the team's, and it may sit anywhere on disk: a vault, a scratch directory, somewhere outside any repository. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.notes.private\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SECRET_INTERACTIVE_TIMEOUT\fR
Bounds a provider read when stdin is a terminal. Default 60s (default: 1m). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsecret.interactive_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SECRET_UNATTENDED_TIMEOUT\fR
Bounds a provider read with no terminal to prompt on. Default 10s (default: 10s). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsecret.unattended_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DIFF_TUI\fR
Opens the interactive viewer when the terminal can draw it. nil = default true. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdiff.tui\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_MAX_DEPTH\fR
How many levels below its root job a fork may land. 0 = unlimited. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.max_depth\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_MAX_LIVE\fR
How many live jobs one root's tree may hold at once, the new one included. 0 = unlimited. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.max_live\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\fR
Bounds a fork that names no \-\-timeout. Zero = no bound. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.default_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_STALE_AFTER\fR
Ends a declared job nobody took and nobody updated for this long, and flags a taken one in `magus ls jobs` and `magus doctor`. Default 2h; 0 = never. Ending a row reads the workspace's own magus.yaml, never user\-global config or the environment (default: 2h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.stale_after\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_RETAIN\fR
How long a job that is over (graded, ended, or exited with its result never collected), and the archive a clear or a delete wrote, stay in the job store once nothing touches them. Default 168h; 0 keeps them forever. Like StaleAfter it reads the workspace's own magus.yaml only (default: 168h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.retain\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_MAX_VALIDATIONS\fR
How many `magus run`s one job tree's leased workers may have going at once; a run past it waits for a seat and says whose run holds it. A run with no lease (the root, a person) is never counted. Default 1; 0 = unlimited. Workspace only, like StaleAfter (default: 1). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.max_validations\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONCURRENCY\fR
Caps concurrent builds; top\-level and in\-process fan\-out share one limiter. Overrides concurrency_profile when set. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconcurrency\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONCURRENCY_PROFILE\fR
Sets the default width relative to the machine: conservative (half the cores), balanced (min(cores, 8), the default) or aggressive (every core). Unset is balanced everywhere; magus reads no environment variable to change this, so CI asks for aggressive explicitly. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconcurrency_profile\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_BROKER\fR
Decides whether a run asks the broker, the per\-user process holding this host's slots, declared memory and shared services: required (refuse a step when none answers), best\-effort (the default: run unarbitrated and say so once), or off (never start or contact one; a run hosts its services itself). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBbroker\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SHUTDOWN_GRACE\fR
Bounds how long the broker and the server take to stop after a first SIGTERM. The broker seats nothing new and waits this long for the runs holding claims or services to finish; the server cancels the runs it adopted and waits this long for them to unwind. A second SIGTERM, or a SIGINT to the broker, stops either at once. Zero stops at once on the first signal; negative is an error (default: 5m). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBshutdown_grace\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MAX_FAILURES\fR
Bounds how many projects may fail before a run stops starting more. Zero, the default, is unlimited: a batch runs everything it can and reports every failure at once. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmax_failures\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TARGET_TIMEOUT\fR
Bounds how long any single target may run before magus cancels it. Zero, the default, means no limit. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtarget_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_STALL_TIMEOUT\fR
Aborts an invocation that is making no progress at all: no target has started, finished, or written a line of output for this long while every selected project's lock is still held. Zero, the default, uses the built\-in 15\-minute window; a negative value turns the watchdog off. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBstall_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_HISTORY_PATH\fR
The path to the runtime\-history JSON used by volatility detection, CI forecaster, graph timing, and bisect. Defaults to $XDG_STATE_HOME/magus/history/v1.json. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBhistory_path\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DRY_RUN\fR
Prints what would run without executing. Equivalent to MAGUS_DRY_RUN=1. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdry_run\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DEFAULT_CHARMS\fR
Execution charms applied to every `magus run` / `magus x` by default, e.g. ["rw"] to make targets write locally without typing :rw. Per\-run :charms stack on top. The ci anchor still strips "rw" (RunCI), so a local `magus run ci` stays read\-only; \-\-no\-default\-charms ignores these for one run. `magus affected` does not apply them, so CI stays read\-only unless explicit. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdefault_charms\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SANDBOX\fR
Off (the default), best\-effort (landlock confines each child where the host has it, magus's own binding checks where it does not), or required (refuse to run, MGS2012, unless the kernel can confine every child: landlock ABI 3). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsandbox.mode\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SANDBOX_ENV_PASSTHROUGH\fR
Adds exact names and prefix patterns such as MISE_* to the built\-in env allowlist. A prefix must be at least three characters and end in "_". Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsandbox.env.passthrough\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_SIGNING_KEY\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the Ed25519 seed that signs remote\-cache writes (see `magus config cache\-key`); env\-only because a signing secret in a committed file is not a secret
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_TOOL_VERSION\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: how tool versions key the cache: project (per project), workspace (once for the workspace), or off (default: project)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_<NAME>_BASE_REF\fR
Per\-VCS base\-ref override, e.g. MAGUS_VCS_GIT_BASE_REF; dynamic pattern, read directly by package vcs
.TP
\fBMAGUS_PROC_SOCKET\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the proc\-server socket a magus process exports for the magus processes it spawns; unix:// URL or bare path, read directly by the process that adopts it
.TP
\fBMAGUS_PROC_TOKEN\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the secret the MAGUS_PROC_SOCKET server requires on every request, exported beside it and inherited only by a nested magus
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SHARD\fR
CI matrix shard ID (e.g. "0"); equivalent to magus run \-\-shard; set by .github/actions/magus
.TP
\fBMAGUS_N_SHARDS\fR
Total shard count for this matrix run; equivalent to magus run \-\-n\-shards; set by .github/actions/magus
.TP
\fBMAGUS_UPDATE_URL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: override the release index URL for `magus self update`; set to a self\-hosted copy of index.json to use a private update channel (default: https://eli.gladman.cc/magus/public/release/index.json)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_STAMPED_LEASE\fR
Set by a shared server on a script it forks for a remote caller, and by an authenticated MCP caller for a child magus: the BAGGAGE lease was stamped by the transport rather than claimed by the spawner. It only downgrades: a missing lease reads as unstamped instead of unbound, never as a grant; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_NO_BOOTSTRAP_EXEC\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: when 1, true or yes, disable the pre\-workspace\-load check that replaces this process with a workspace\-local ./magus found by walking up from the working directory (or \-\-root); set it to force the binary actually invoked to run instead, e.g. while debugging that binary itself (default: false)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_OFFLINE\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: when set to anything but 0 or false, a remote\-spell fetch and every std/http request a script sends fail with a named error instead of sending a request, and the lifecycle provider is not asked: `magus describe tools` replays its stored answer or reads unknown (offline) (default: false)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DIFFTOOL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the command, taking two paths, that `\-\-then file <path> diff` compares a cached artifact with (default: $DIFFTOOL, then git diff \-\-no\-index)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_VIEWER_URL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: base URL of the log viewer page a live run opens, for a self\-hosted mirror (default: the hosted log viewer)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONSOLE_DIR\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: directory of the built console the LAN share serves (default: <root>/console/gen)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_PPROF\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: write Go profiles for one invocation, as kind:path pairs (cpu, mem, trace), comma separated
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_TOKEN\fR
Env\-only: the secret reference shipped harness spells name for the MCP bearer token; the environment secret provider reads it from this variable
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_BUZZ_PURE\fR
Set internally by the buzz MCP tool for its forked transform worker; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_CLIENT\fR
Set internally by the client MCP tool for its forked worker; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_CLIENT_HOST\fR
Set internally by the client MCP tool: the calling client's name, stamped onto the worker's activity trail; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_CLIENT_LEASE\fR
Set internally by the client MCP tool: the calling client's job lease, or empty when the transport stamped none; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_S3_BUCKET\fR
Env\-only: the bucket the aws/s3\-cache spell stores remote\-cache artifacts in
.TP
\fBMAGUS_S3_ENDPOINT\fR
Env\-only: the S3\-compatible endpoint the aws/s3\-cache spell talks to (default: https://s3.<region>.amazonaws.com)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LEVEL\fR
Set by magus for the processes it spawns: the magus recursion depth, like make's MAKELEVEL; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INVOCATION_ANCESTORS\fR
Set by magus for the processes it spawns: the comma\-separated invocations a nested magus runs underneath; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_BOOTSTRAP_EXEC_DONE\fR
Set by magus when it replaces itself with a workspace\-local ./magus, so the replacement never hops again; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SYMBOL_INDEX\fR
Set by magus for a spell's symbol indexer op: the path the indexer writes its SCIP index to; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_WORKSPACE_ROOT\fR
Set by magus for a spell's symbol indexer op: the workspace root the index's paths are relative to; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_MODE\fR
Set by `magus diff` for the advice script it runs; the two halves of one feature, not a setting, and either may be renamed without notice
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_BASE_BRANCH\fR
Set by `magus diff` alongside MAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_MODE; not a setting
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fBmagus.yaml\fR, \fB.magus.yaml\fR
Configuration file. Searched in CWD, workspace root, and
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magus/ in ascending priority order. Both plain and
dot\-prefixed names are accepted; having both in the same directory is an error.
.TP
\fB.magus\-cache/\fR
Content\-addressed build cache in the workspace root. Override with
MAGUS_CACHE_DIR.
